WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.355
I've become very very interested
in the idea

00:00:04.355 --> 00:00:06.900
of playing in games that have no finish lines.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:15.040
Some games have finish lines, 
baseball, football.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.600
Getting a part is a finish line.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.910
You audition, 
there's a beginning, middle and end.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.400
There's rehearsal and practice.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.939
There's showing up for the audition

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:31.508
and you either win or you lose, 
and then it's over.

00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:33.090
That is finite.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.200
But one's career is infinite.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.400
There's no end.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.989
It's like our lives are finite

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:41.100
but life is infinite.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.860
People come and
people go but life continues.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.360
Theater.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.307
Actors come and actors go 
but theater continues.

00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:48.329
It's infinite.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.000
You don't win theater.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.039
You win a part.
But what happens once you get the part?

00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:57.165
The finite game is over.

00:00:57.165 --> 00:00:59.800
Now you enter the infinite game, 
you have to be able to convert.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.359
And the reason this is important,

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:05.719
and I've seen this unfortunately so many times,

00:01:05.719 --> 00:01:08.500
from a young age
all you wanted to do was get to Broadway.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.600
And then you get to Broadway,
and then what?

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.800
You've devoted your entire life to one finite goal

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.400
and when you get there,
the immediate response is depression

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:23.520
because I spent 15 years of my life
for this one thing

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.580
and I got it
and now I don't know what to do next.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.900
Like what do, 
get to Broadway again?!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.439
It doesn't have the same ambition.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:36.440
It doesn't have the same passion,

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.360
that you've devoted,

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.280
you're from Fargo, North Dakota

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.800
and that's all you wanted to do is
get out of Fargo and make it to Broadway

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:44.820
and you made it.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.900
It doesn't have the same kind of passion.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.360
and this is because these are
finite goals.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.812
There's a lot of studies that have been done with

00:01:54.812 --> 00:01:57.630
athletes who have finite goals.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.279
To become the greatest X in the world.

00:02:00.279 --> 00:02:02.789
So Andre Agassi was one of these athletes.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.909
He wanted to become the
greatest tennis player that ever lived.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:06.544
So guess what?

00:02:06.544 --> 00:02:09.900
Everyone in his life
he would view them through,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.900
how do you help me get to that?

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.049
Everything was
how does this help me get to that?

00:02:16.049 --> 00:02:17.282
Everything was a transaction,

00:02:17.282 --> 00:02:18.685
how do you help me move to there,

00:02:18.685 --> 00:02:19.620
and then you know what happens?

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.010
He achieved it,
he became the greatest tennis player in the world

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.820
and you know what happened immediately after?

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.776
Depression.

00:02:26.776 --> 00:02:30.900
Michael Phelps set out to become the most medaled Olympian in history

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.970
Do you know what?
He achieved it.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.399
You know what happened immediately after?

00:02:35.399 --> 00:02:36.820
Depression.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.900
They spend their whole life working for
one goal.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.483
Though most will never get it,

00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:43.799
the few that do,
don't know what to do next

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:47.600
because their goals were finite.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.859
Their goals were finite.

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:52.900
And so there are finite components to your career

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.130
but your career should be infinite.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:00.200
So yes, of course you have to win
the finite game.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.950
You have to get the part.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.100
But immediately when you get the part

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.000
now you convert to infinite.

